{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Elohim has gathered up my reproach</b> — He brought it into a place where it would not be seen. And similarly: וְלֹא יֵאָסֵף הַבַּיְתָה (Exodus 9:19); וְכוֹכָבִים אָסְפוּ נָגְהָם (Joel 2:10); וִירֵחֵךְ לֹא יֵאָסֵף (Isaiah 60:20) — it will not be gathered, that is, not concealed — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 30:23). And Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 30:23) it has the sense of cutting off, as in וְנֶאֶסְפָה שִׂמְחָה וָגִיל. But the correct view is that of Onkelos (Onkelos on Genesis 30:23), that all of them are in the sense of gathering and assembling in their plain meaning, from the root of וַיַּאַסְפוּ אֶת הַשְּׂלָו (Numbers 11:32), כִּי מְאַסְפָיו יֹאכְלוּהוּ (Isaiah 62:9). And death is called אֲסִיפָה because one is gathered to his dead ancestors; וְלֹא יֵאָסֵף הַבַּיְתָה — to be gathered to the people of his house; and אָסְפוּ נָגְהָם — because they gathered their light within themselves and did not emit their light outward, or because they were gathered to their tent which is theirs in the firmament of the heavens. And one says אֲסִיפָה בַּחֶרְפָּה — that it would be gathered and not scattered among the children of men, so that they would no longer speak of it in the streets."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:36:59.218107784Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}